    <string name="lessons_title">Lessons</string>
    <string name="lesson_basics">Cube basics</string>
    <string name="lesson_basics_summary">Pieces, centres, move names and how to hold the cube.</string>
    <string name="lesson_basics_p1">Centres never move: each side's centre tells the side's colour.</string>
    <string name="lesson_basics_p2">An edge has two colours, a corner three. A piece belongs between the centres of its colours.</string>
    <string name="lesson_basics_p3">A letter tells what turns: R the right side, L the left side, U the top layer, D the bottom layer, F the front side, B the back side. R: the right side up, R' down, R2 half a turn. U: the top layer to the left, U' to the right.</string>
    <string name="lesson_basics_p4">Hold white on top and green in front, and the cube on screen matches yours.</string>
    <string name="lesson_basics_practice">Try moves on the free cube</string>
    <string name="lesson_tip">Tip</string>
    <string name="lesson_practice">Practise this stage</string>
    <string name="lesson_play">Play the sequence</string>
    <string name="lesson_1_summary">Four white edges as a cross on top.</string>
    <string name="lesson_2_summary">White corners into place with the trigger.</string>
    <string name="lesson_3_summary">Second layer: four edges into the middle layer.</string>
    <string name="lesson_4_summary">A yellow cross on top with one sequence.</string>
    <string name="lesson_5_summary">Yellow edges into their places.</string>
    <string name="lesson_6_summary">Yellow corners into their places.</string>
    <string name="lesson_7_summary">The last corners the right way – the cube is done.</string>
    <string name="lesson_1_tip">Check the sides too: each edge's other colour sits next to its own centre.</string>
    <string name="lesson_2_tip">The trigger R' D' R D comes back in the last stage.</string>
    <string name="lesson_3_tip">Look for a top edge with no yellow on it.</string>
    <string name="lesson_4_tip">Look at the edges only – the corners don't matter yet.</string>
    <string name="lesson_5_tip">First turn the top layer until two edges match their centres.</string>
    <string name="lesson_6_tip">The sequence leaves the front right corner where it is.</string>
    <string name="lesson_7_tip">The lower layers get mixed up on the way and come back – don't turn the whole cube.</string>
